    "text": "Iu on ealdum dagum w\u00e6s sum rice cyning namcu\u00f0 on worulde, Asuerus gehaten.\nAnd se h\u00e6fde cynerice east fram Indian o\u00f0 E\u00feiopian lande; \u00fe\u00e6t is fram easteweardan \u00feissere worulde\nHundtwelftig scira he so\u00f0lice h\u00e6fde and seofon scira, swa swa us secga\u00f0 bec, on his anwealde ealle him\nOn \u00feam \u00feriddan geare his cynerices he het gewyrcan wundorlice feorme hundteontig daga on an and\nUs is earfo\u00f0e to secgenne \u00fea seltcu\u00f0an m\u00e6r\u00f0a on gyldenum beddum and agrafenum fatum, gyldene and\nSe cyning bebead \u00feam gebeorum eallum, \u00fe\u00e6t hi bli\u00fee w\u00e6ron \u00e6t his gebeorscipe and \u00fe\u00e6t \u00e6lc mann\nAc \u00fea byrlas scencton be \u00fe\u00e6s cyninges gesetnysse \u00e6lcum men genoh name, \u00fe\u00e6t he wolde.\nHis cwen hatte Vasthi, seo w\u00e6s swi\u00f0e wlitig.\nHeo worhte eac feorme mid fulre m\u00e6r\u00f0e eallum \u00feam wifmannum, \u00fee heo wolde habban to hire m\u00e6r\u00fee\nSe cyning \u00fea het on \u00feam seofo\u00f0an d\u00e6ge, \u00fea \u00fea he bli\u00fee w\u00e6s betwux his gebeorum, his seofon\nAnd he wolde \u00e6teowian hire wlite his \u00feegnum, for\u00fean \u00fee heo w\u00e6s swi\u00fee wlitig on hiwe.\n\u00dea eodon \u00fea bur\u00f0enas and abudon \u00fe\u00e6re cwene \u00fe\u00e6s cyninges h\u00e6se.\nAc heo hit forsoc and nolde gehyrsumian him to his willan.\nSe cyning \u00fea sona swi\u00f0e wear\u00f0 geyrsod, \u00fe\u00e6t heo hine forseah on swylcere gegaderunge, and befran his\n\u00dea andwyrdon sona sume his ealdormen of Medan and of Persan, \u00fee him mid druncon: Seo cwen\n\u00d0onne ure wif geaxia\u00f0 be \u00feisum wordum \u00e6t ham, hu seo cwen forseah hire cynehlaford, \u00feonne willa\u00f0\nAc gif \u00fee swa ge\u00feinc\u00f0, leof, gesette \u00feisne dom, \u00fe\u00e6t ealle Medas cwe\u00f0a\u00f0 anmodum ge\u00feeahte and eac \u00fea\nAnd se cyning Asuerus \u00feisne r\u00e6d underfeng, and man cydde \u00fea geond eall \u00fe\u00e6s cyninges willan.\nAnd Vasthi geseah \u00fea, \u00fe\u00e6t heo forsewen w\u00e6s.\nHit wear\u00fe \u00fea gecweden \u00feurh \u00fe\u00e6s cyninges witan, \u00fe\u00e6t man ofaxode on eallum his rice, gif \u00e6nig m\u00e6den\nAnd se cyning \u00fea het embe \u00fe\u00e6t beon swi\u00f0e.\nOn \u00feam dagum w\u00e6s an Iudeisc \u00feegen on \u00fe\u00e6re byrig Susa, Mardocheus gehaten.\nSe gelyfde so\u00f0lice on \u00feone lifigendan god \u00e6fter Moyses \u00e6, and he mid him h\u00e6fde his bro\u00f0or dohtor,\nAnd he hi gefor\u00f0ode on f\u00e6gerum \u00feeawum \u00e6fter godes \u00e6 and his ege symle and h\u00e6fde hi for dohtor,\nSeo wear\u00f0 \u00fea gebroht and bes\u00e6d \u00feam cyninge.\nAnd he hi sceawode and him sona gelicode hire f\u00e6gra nebwlite and lufode hi swi\u00f0e ofer ealle \u00fea o\u00f0re,\nAc heo ne moste na for Mardocheo nateshwon hire cynn ameldian, ne \u00feam cyninge secgan, hwilcere\nMardocheus \u00fea folgode \u00feam m\u00e6dene to hirede and hire gym\u00e6ne h\u00e6fde holdlice symle, wolde gewitan,\nHeo w\u00e6s swi\u00f0e wlitig on wundorlicre gef\u00e6gernysse and swi\u00fee lufigendlic eallum onlociendum and\nAnd se cyning hi genam to cwene \u00fea and gesette \u00feone cynehelm on hire heafod sona, \u00fee Vasthi \u00e6r\nHe het \u00fea gearcian to heora gyftum swi\u00f0e m\u00e6nigfealde m\u00e6r\u00f0a, swa him mihte gerisan.\nAnd \u00e6fter heora gewunan he gewifode \u00fea swa be his witena r\u00e6de on heora gewitnysse and his folc\nHit gelamp \u00fea si\u00f0\u00f0an \u00e6fter litlum firste, \u00fe\u00e6t twegen his bur\u00f0ena mid bealuwe afyllede woldon\n\u00dea wear\u00f0 hit sona cu\u00fe \u00feam Mardocheo, \u00fe\u00e6re cwene f\u00e6deran.\nAnd he hit \u00fea cydde ardlice hire and heo \u00feam cyninge for\u00f0.\nAnd man afunde mid him swutele tacnu, \u00fe\u00e6t hi swa woldon don, and hi sylfe s\u00e6don, \u00fe\u00e6t hi swa\nAnd man aheng hi begen on healicum gealgan.\nAnd Mardocheus \u00fea wear\u00f0 \u00feurh \u00fea micclan hlyde cu\u00f0 \u00feam cyninge for \u00f0\u00e6re gecy\u00fenysse.\nHit w\u00e6s \u00fea gewunelic swi\u00f0e wislice, \u00fe\u00e6t man gesette on cranice \u00e6lc \u00fe\u00e6ra d\u00e6da, \u00fee gedon w\u00e6s mid\n\u00dea het he awritan, hu hine gewarnede Mardocheus se \u00feegen, \u00fe\u00e6t hit on geminde w\u00e6re.\nSum ealdorman w\u00e6s \u00fea Aman gehaten, \u00feone geuferode se cyning ofer ealle his \u00feegnas and ofer his\nAnd ealle his men si\u00f0\u00f0an him anum abugon, buton Mardocheus for his micclum ge\u00feing\u00feum nolde him\n\u00dea geseah Aman, \u00fe\u00e6t he hine forseah, and he h\u00e6fde ofaxod \u00e6t o\u00f0rum mannum \u00e6r, \u00fe\u00e6t he w\u00e6s\nAman \u00fea smeade swicollice embe \u00fe\u00e6t, hu he eall Iudeisc cynn fordyde \u00e6tg\u00ebdere, \u00fee godes \u00e6 heoldon\nAnd \u00feu wel wast, leof, \u00fe\u00e6t hit wile hearmian \u00feinum cynerice heora receleasnysse, gyf him man ne\nL\u00e6t hi ealle fordon and ic gedo, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feu h\u00e6fst tyn \u00feusend punda to \u00feinum mydercum.\nSe cyning \u00fea sona slypte his beah of and forgeaf Amane and be \u00feam mancynne cw\u00e6\u00fe: Hafa \u00fee \u00fe\u00e6t\nAman \u00fea sona, swa he \u00feis gehyrde, dihte gewritu be \u00feam Iudeiscum to \u00e6lcere scire, \u00fee hi on\nMardocheus \u00fea micclum wear\u00f0 geangsumod and for his agenum magum get micele swi\u00f0or, \u00feonne for\n\u00dea bebead seo cwen, \u00fe\u00e6t hire cynn eall sceolde f\u00e6stan \u00fereo dagas on an and godes fultum biddan.\nAnd heo sylf eall swa eac swylce f\u00e6ste, biddende \u00e6t gode, \u00fe\u00e6t he geburge \u00feam folce and eallum \u00feam\n\u00dea eode seo cwen \u00e6fter \u00feam f\u00e6stene swi\u00f0e f\u00e6geres hiwes \u00e6tforan \u00feam cyninge.\nAnd he swi\u00f0e bli\u00f0e bicnode hire to mid his cynegyrde and gecw\u00e6\u00fe \u00feas word: Hw\u00e6s bytst \u00feu, la\nSeo cwen cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fea to him: Leof cynehlaford, ic wille, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feu beo \u00e6t minum gebeorscipe, \u00feu, leof, and\n\u00dea het se cyning clypian Aman and het, \u00fe\u00e6t he w\u00e6re gehyrsum \u00fe\u00e6re cwene to hire willan, to hire\nAnd Aman \u00fea gecyrde sona to his inne.\nMardocheus \u00fea s\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6r ute and nolde alutan, ne lyffettan \u00feam Amane.\n\u00dea wear\u00f0 he swi\u00fee gram \u00feam godes \u00feegene and cw\u00e6\u00fe to his cnihtum, \u00fe\u00e6t him forcu\u00felic \u00feuhte, \u00fe\u00e6t se\nSe cyning me wur\u00f0a\u00fe, swa swa gewita\u00fe ealle, and seo cwen ne gela\u00feode n\u00ebnne o\u00f0erne to hire butan\nNu \u00feing\u00fe me, \u00fe\u00e6t ic n\u00e6bbe n\u00e6nne wur\u00f0scipe on life, swa lange swa Mardocheus me nele abugan.\n\u00dea cw\u00e6don his magas, \u00fe\u00e6t he macian sceolde \u00e6nne heagan gealgan and habban hine gearwe and\nAnd he \u00fea swa dyde be heora dyslican r\u00e6de.\nHit gelamp \u00fea on \u00fe\u00e6re nihte, \u00fe\u00e6t se cyning l\u00e6g w\u00e6ccende lange on forannihte.\nAnd he het \u00fea for\u00f0beran \u00feone cranic fram his yldrena dagum and r\u00e6dan \u00e6tforan him, o\u00f0 \u00f0\u00e6t he fulge\nMan him r\u00e6dde \u00fea fela \u00fe\u00e6s \u00fee gefyrn gelamp, o\u00f0 \u00f0\u00e6t hit becom \u00fe\u00e6rto, hu his burcnihtas woldon hine\n\u00dea befran se cyning his cnihtas and cw\u00e6\u00fe: Hwylce mede h\u00e6fde Mardocheus for \u00feam, \u00fe\u00e6t he swa\nHis cnihtas him andwyrdon and cw\u00e6don him \u00feus to: Leof cynehlaford, ne com him nan \u00feing to \u00feance,\nHw\u00e6t, \u00fea on \u00e6rnemergen com Aman to \u00feam cyninge, wolde, \u00fe\u00e6t he hete ahon Mardocheum.\nAc se cyning axode hine sona and cw\u00eb\u00f0: Hw\u00e6t \u00feing\u00f0 \u00fee, Aman, hw\u00e6t hit mage beon, \u00fe\u00e6t ic gedon\n\u00dea wende Aman to gewissan \u00feinge, \u00fe\u00e6t se cyning wolde wur\u00feian hine swi\u00f0or and n\u00e6nne o\u00feerne, and\nAnd l\u00e6de sum ealdormann hine geond \u00feas burh and secge \u00feam burhmannum, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feus beo gewur\u00f0od\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00fe se cyning to Amane: Ic cwe\u00f0e, \u00fe\u00e6t ic wille, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feu genime Mardocheum and \u00feisne\nAman \u00fea dyde swa mid sorhfullum mode and gel\u00e6dde Mardocheum m\u00e6rlice gescrydne and mid\nSe cyning \u00fea sende sona \u00e6fter Amane and he un\u00feances \u00fea com to \u00fe\u00e6re cwene feorme.\nAnd se cyning Asuerus swi\u00fee bli\u00f0e w\u00e6s \u00fe\u00e6s d\u00e6ges mid \u00fe\u00e6re cwene Hester and cw\u00e6\u00f0 hire \u00feus to:\nHester seo cwen \u00fea cw\u00e6\u00f0 to \u00feam cyninge \u00feus: Ic bidde \u00fee, la leof, mines agenes lifes and mines\nWe synd ealle bel\u00ebwde to ure lifleaste, \u00fe\u00e6t we beon toheawene mid heardum swurdum, \u00fe\u00e6t ure\nSe cyning \u00fea befran \u00fea cwene \u00feus eft: Hw\u00e6t is se manna and hwilcere mihte, \u00fee \u00feas d\u00e6da \u00e6fre dorste\nHeo cw\u00e6\u00f0 to andsware: Us is se wyrsta feond witodlice \u00fees Aman, \u00fee h\u00e6f\u00f0 gecweden andagan, \u00fe\u00e6t\n\u00dea ablicgde Aman unbli\u00feum andwlitan and ne mihte na acuman \u00fe\u00e6s cyninges graman, ne he ne dorste\nAnd se cyning aras hra\u00fee gehathyrt and eode him sona ut binnon his \u00e6ppeltun swilce for r\u00e6dinge.\nAc he hra\u00fee sona eft eode him inn.\nAnd efne Aman \u00fea ni\u00feer afeallen to \u00fe\u00e6re cwene fotum, \u00fe\u00e6t heo him gefultumode to his agenum feore.\n\u00dea oflicode \u00feam cyninge, \u00fe\u00e6t he l\u00e6g hire swa gehende.\nAnd \u00fea cnihtas oncneowon \u00fe\u00e6s cyninges micclan graman and gefengon \u00feone Aman and hine\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 an \u00feara burcnihta to \u00feam cyninge \u00feus: La leof cynehlaford, an lang gealga st\u00e6nt \u00e6t Amanes\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 se cyning to andsware: Ahoh hine \u00fe\u00e6ron.\nAnd hi sona swa dydon mid swi\u00f0licum ofste, ahengon \u00feone Aman on \u00feam healican gealgan, \u00fee he\nAnd \u00fe\u00e6s cyninges yrre wear\u00f0 \u00fea geli\u00feegod.\n\u00dea cydde seo cwen eall be hire cynne hire cynehlaforde, hwanon heo cumen w\u00e6s, and be Mardocheo,\nAnd he eode \u00fea inn toforan \u00feam cyninge.\nAnd se cyning him sealde sona \u00feone beah, \u00fee he genam of Amane, him to wur\u00f0scipe, and he\nAnd he his \u00e6hta bet\u00e6hte \u00fe\u00e6re cwene to h\u00e6bbenne.\nSeo cwen \u00fea aleat to \u00fe\u00e6s cyninges fotum mid agotenum tearum, mid godes ege onbryrd, and b\u00e6d hire\nSe cyning \u00fea andwyrde \u00fe\u00e6re cwene \u00feus and eac Mardocheo swi\u00f0e mildelice: Aman ic aheng and his\nHwa dear nu gedyrstl\u00e6can, \u00fe\u00e6t he derige \u00feam folce?\nAwrita\u00f0 nu gewritu, be\u00feam \u00fee ge willa\u00fe, \u00fe\u00e6t eall beo aidlod Amanes sirwung ongean \u00feam Iudeiscum\nAc ic swi\u00f0or wille, \u00fe\u00e6t man ofslea eac Amanes magas for his micclan swicdome.\n\u00deis wear\u00f0 \u00fea gefor\u00feod and hi on fri\u00fee wunedon \u00feurh \u00fe\u00e6re cwene \u00feingunge, \u00fee him \u00fea geheolp and\n\u00dea Iudeiscan eac wundorlice blissodon, \u00fe\u00e6t hi swilcne forespr\u00e6can him afunden h\u00e6fdon, and heoldon\nMardocheus eac micclum w\u00e6s gewur\u00feod and swi\u00f0e geuferod for his eadmodnysse, swa swa Aman\nAnd se cyning wear\u00f0 gerihtl\u00e6ht \u00feurh \u00fe\u00e6re cwene geleafan gode to wur\u00f0mynte, \u00fee ealle \u00feing gewylt.\nAnd he herode god, \u00fee hine geuferode and to cyninge geceas ofer swilcne anweald.\nAnd he w\u00e6s rihtwis and r\u00e6df\u00e6st on weorcum.\nAnd he h\u00e6fde o\u00feerne naman Artarxerses.\nSy wuldor and lof \u00feam welwillendan gode, se \u00fee \u00e6fre rixa\u00f0 on ecnysse.\nAmen.",
